# VideoBrief — Worktrees

Use **in-repo** worktrees under `.worktrees/` via the repo scripts. Do **not** hand-roll `git worktree add` to `~/.cursor/worktrees/` — that path needs sandbox escalation and breaks on trivial tasks.

## When to use

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Parallel agents / conflicting edits | Create worktree |
| Copy, CSS, one-field i18n, no other agent active | Edit primary checkout — **skip worktree** |

## Commands (run from repo root)

```bash
.cursor/worktree-create.sh [name] [start-ref]   # prints WORKTREE_PATH
.cursor/worktree-status.sh [name]               # drift + merge previews (readonly)
.cursor/worktree-sync.sh <name>                  # merge primary into wt/<name> (catch up)
.cursor/worktree-apply.sh <name>                # merge wt/<name> into current branch
.cursor/worktree-delete.sh <name>               # remove worktree + branch
```

After `worktree-create.sh`, do **all** reads, edits, and shell for that task in `WORKTREE_PATH` until apply or delete. Cursor’s default cwd is the **primary checkout** — every shell command must `cd` to the worktree (or set `working_directory` to that absolute path). Run `pwd` if unsure. Do not edit the primary tree for a worktree task.

Before creating, check for an existing worktree: `git worktree list`. If the user points at a current worktree, or one already exists for this work, **keep using it** — do not open a second worktree. Reuse `.worktrees/<name>` **as-is** when present (even if `main` is ahead).

**Do not catch up the worktree onto primary/`main` while parallel work is still active.** No manual `git merge main`, `git rebase main`, `git pull`, or `git reset --hard` onto main during implementation. Other worktrees and later main commits are usually isolated — stay on the worktree’s current HEAD.

**After sibling worktrees land**, the remaining worktree is often behind. Run `worktree-status.sh`, then `worktree-sync.sh <name>` to merge primary into the worktree, resolve conflicts **in the worktree**, test there, and only then `worktree-apply.sh`. Do not sync preemptively if other agents are still working in parallel on sibling worktrees.

`.worktrees/` is typically gitignored / tool-ignored. Grep and Glob from the primary root will miss worktree files. Read, write, and search with absolute paths under `WORKTREE_PATH`.

## Setup (must finish in seconds)

`worktree-create.sh` runs `.cursor/setup-worktree-unix.sh` inside the new worktree:

1. Copy `.env.local` from primary
2. **Hardlink-clone** `node_modules` from primary (preferred) — no registry, no store write
3. Only if primary has no usable `node_modules`: offline `pnpm install --frozen-store` with a **90s timeout**

Run create in the **default sandbox** (do **not** request `full_network` / `all` just for create).

**Why not bare `pnpm install` in the sandbox:** the sandbox cannot write `~/.local/share/pnpm/store` and remaps pnpm toward an in-repo `.pnpm-store` that is often incomplete. Install then hangs on proxy fetches despite `--prefer-offline`. Never “wait it out.”

If setup hangs or fails: kill it, ensure primary has a complete `pnpm install`, then either re-run `worktree-create.sh` (reuses the worktree) or:

```bash
ROOT_WORKTREE_PATH="$(pwd)" bash .worktrees/<name>/../../.cursor/setup-worktree-unix.sh
# or from repo root:
ROOT_WORKTREE_PATH="$PWD" bash -c 'cd .worktrees/<name> && bash "$ROOT_WORKTREE_PATH/.cursor/setup-worktree-unix.sh"'
```

If an existing worktree is missing env only: `cp .env.local .worktrees/<name>/.env.local` from repo root.

Do **not** run `db:migrate` from a worktree against shared Supabase unless that is the task.

Apply one worktree at a time **only when the human asks** (after their improve/UI pass). If `worktree-status.sh` shows `behind>0` or `apply=conflict`, sync first. Then: apply → type-check, lint, test in primary checkout. **Do not delete** — wait for `/worktree-delete`.

`/ship-feature` follows this policy: pick `CHECKOUT` (primary or `.worktrees/<name>`), pass that absolute path into every specialist Task prompt, implement/check/review there, then **stop with READY** until the user says `/worktree-apply` (or equivalent). See `.cursor/skills/ship-feature/SKILL.md`.
